research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.proof-contracts.json:444:          "evidence": "The five-term polynomial expansion cancels over Z2; any coboundary would force c(0,0)=c(0,1)=c(1,0) and then delta c(1,1,1)=0 despite beta(1,1,1)=1. The listed background has delta_a B=1, and after g=(1,0,0,0) it has a prime first edge 0, B prime=0, and beta(a prime)=0."
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.proof-contracts.json:447:      "finite_checks_disposition": "This is a direct calculation on one tetrahedron and does not classify all finite 2-group backgrounds."
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-15.notes.md:11:Claim: defines exact finite semisimple ordinary fusion-category data and a semistrict finite semisimple fusion-2-category presentation, including associativity/pentagon, units, rigidity/duals, simple unit, and the distinction between simple and tensor-invertible objects. It states explicitly that unitarity and physical realization are not implied. Conventions: ordinary fusion category uses the exact local finite semisimple tensor-category interface; the higher branch uses the Douglas–Reutter Gray-monoid convention and their finite semisimple 2-category/idempotent-completeness definitions. Mathematical dependencies are `def-fusion-and-multifusion-category` and `def-monoidal-category`; no physical supplier is used. `dependency_level: 0`.
