research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.pages.json:160:        "reference": "items/thm-aqft-finite-background-two-groupoid-coherence.md",
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.pages.json:161:        "statement": "For every finite ordered simplicial complex and finite data $(G,A,\\rho,\\beta)$ in the background gauge $2$-groupoid definition, its displayed operations define a finite $2$-groupoid, including the relative version for every subcomplex and fixed boundary field. Its raw $1$-arrows are not identified by their effects on background objects. For $x=(a,B)$,\n\n$$\n\\pi_2(\\mathcal B(K),x)=\\ker(\\delta_a:C^0(K;A)\\to C^1(K;A)).\n$$\n\nIf $S_x$ is the finite set of raw $1$-automorphisms at $x$, each $2$-isomorphism class in $S_x$ has $|\\operatorname{im}\\delta_a|$ elements, and\n\n$$\n|\\pi_1(\\mathcal B(K),x)|=|S_x|/|\\operatorname{im}\\delta_a|.\n$$\n\nThe same assertions hold relatively, using vertex and edge cochains vanishing on the subcomplex. On a single vertex, $\\pi_1=G$ and $\\pi_2=A$, with associator determined by $\\beta$.",
