research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:5:Owned A/B pair: **qftx-two-group-cochains** and **qftx-two-group-cochains-examples**, category **quantum-field-theory-mathematics**, mathematics library. The complete design at research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md § “Finite 2-Group Background Cochains and Consistency” (line 177) calls for a finite simplicial background with local coefficients and a Postnikov cocycle, explicit gauge transformations, and closure/composition. The matching A/B rows in research/plan-spec.json have the same IDs, titles, category, library, and page edges; A requires no earlier page, and B requires A. The batch-13 manifest and the prose scaffold both had empty item inventories as preauthoring placeholders. No design/plan conflict was found.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:7:The dependency-level record gives batch 13 level 0 with requires []. The item DAG is **def-aqft-two-group-background** at level 0, **thm-aqft-two-group-background-consistency** at level 1, and the two planned B examples at level 1 because each uses only the A definition. The B-page-to-A-page edge is within this batch, not a cross-batch edge. The planned direct page consumers outside this batch are **qftx-finite-symmetry-gauging** (batch 14) and **qftx-two-group-symmetry-backgrounds** (batch 38); their exact interface use remains for their owning authors to check.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:9:## Completed item: def-aqft-two-group-background
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:11:**Claim and conventions.** Defines a finite skeletal 2-group from finite (G,A,rho,beta) data, with A additive, left action rho, normalized inhomogeneous 3-cocycle beta, ordered simplicial complexes, vertex-first local coefficients, flat edge labels a_ij a_jk=a_ik, the twisted differential, the constraint delta_a B=a^* beta, and representative-level 0-form and 1-form gauge formulas. It defines cocycle equivalence by normalized 2-coboundaries and names [beta] the Postnikov class in this skeletal model; additivity gives reflexivity, symmetry, and transitivity. The associator is directed from (gh)k to g(hk) with label beta(g,h,k), so the tetrahedron equation is rho(a_ij)B_jkl-B_ikl+B_ijl-B_ijk=beta(a_ij,a_jk,a_kl). The representative change beta -> beta+delta_rho c, B -> B+a^*c is checked inline by flat-pullback naturality.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:13:**Placement and dependencies.** Carrier: items/def-aqft-two-group-background.md; A page: **qftx-two-group-cochains**; domain mathematics, library mathematics, dependency_level 0, no deps, and an empty dependency_roles map. No Choice principle or imported mathematical supplier is used.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:17:- Benini, Córdova, and Hsin, [§2.3, PDF pp. 18–19](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1803.09336): simplicial flatness, the twisted tetrahedron equation, and 0-/1-form gauge transformations. Disposition: included for the background interface; their undetermined zeta cochain and unexpanded composition law are replaced by the local explicit formulas.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:18:- Baez and Lauda, [§8.3, PDF pp. 54–59](https://arxiv.org/pdf/math/0307200): the skeletal (G,H,action,a) structure and the associator/pentagon 3-cocycle relation. Disposition: included for the mathematical coherence convention; it does not supply simplicial QFT backgrounds.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:19:- Schäfer-Nameki, [§§2.5 and 2.8.1, printed pp. 23–33](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2305.18296v2): discrete cochain backgrounds, a Postnikov constraint, and the distinction from anomaly data. Disposition: context-only for the local mathematical construction.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:27:## Completed item: thm-aqft-two-group-background-consistency
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:29:**Claim and conventions.** Proves that for flat edge labels and a 2-cochain satisfying the Definition's twisted tetrahedron equation, every explicitly written vertex/edge transformation preserves flatness and the equation. The composite of (g,lambda) followed by (h,mu) has vertex component hg and the five-term edge label nu in the item. A reverse transformation is constructed for each source background, and induced gauge maps compose associatively as functions.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:31:**Placement and dependencies.** Carrier: items/thm-aqft-two-group-background-consistency.md; A page qftx-two-group-cochains; domain mathematics, library mathematics, dependency_level 1, with the single dependency def-aqft-two-group-background assigned role mathematical-premise. No other supplier, Choice assumption, or physical premise is used.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:33:**Proof route.** Step 1.1 checks transformed flatness; 1.2 expands the local-coefficient differential squares; 1.3 writes the zeta coboundary discrepancy as the signed sum of four exact bar-cocycle identities; 1.4 concludes equation preservation. Step 2.1 derives the composition parameter by adding the five associator/edge-morphism labels; 2.2 uses the scalar pentagon for triangle coherence. Step 3.1 constructs an inverse edge cochain for each fixed source background. The strict proof contract and finite smoke checks passed.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:37:**Scope correction.** An exploratory stronger claim that the two raw parenthesized parameter arrays differ only by the vertex cochain sigma_i=beta(k_i,h_i,g_i) was not retained: after correcting the parenthesization in a sign-sensitive Z3-coefficient check, the first failing sample had edge 1–2 with left label 0, right label 2, and predicted delta-sigma label 0. The planned contract requires background preservation and a pairwise composition formula, both proved and checked; the final theorem does not assert that extra raw-parameter identity.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:45:### ex-aqft-two-group-twisted-local-coefficient-background
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:47:Defines the split case on one ordered tetrahedron with G=Z2, A=Z3, the sign action rho_1(t)=-t, beta=0, and a flat edge cochain from vertex potentials. It verifies that lambda_01=1 shifts the zero 2-cochain to the two-face cocycle B_012=B_013=1. Placement is the B page. Its sole logical dependency is def-aqft-two-group-background at dependency_level 1, role mathematical-premise. The computation is local and uses no external source, physical assumption, or Choice principle.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:49:### ex-aqft-two-group-postnikov-background
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-13.notes.md:51:Defines beta(g,h,k)=ghk for G=A=Z2 with trivial action, proves the normalized 3-cocycle identity and non-coboundary property directly, constructs a flat tetrahedron background with delta_a B=1, and explicitly checks the transformed data under g=(1,0,0,0). It includes a labelled TikZ tetrahedron whose incidence is supplementary to the algebraic verification. Placement is the B page. Its sole logical dependency is def-aqft-two-group-background at dependency_level 1, role mathematical-premise. This is a finite mathematical example, not a physical anomaly statement.
