research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-16.notes.md:36:The local exactness result `lem-aqft-invariant-quotient-exactness` proves the canonical map from invariant operators modulo invariant relations to invariant classes in the raw quotient, using only the exact finite rational-module statement of the imported complete-reducibility/Reynolds theorem. The field-redefinition proposition treats one chosen order at a time in a finite truncated formal parameter, requires the stated compact-support/no-boundary functional convention, and includes the higher-order remainder. The later theorem states quantum on-shell amplitude equivalence only for a specified finite regulator, transformed measure/Jacobian and sources, and a stable-particle LSZ data set with simple poles and nonzero overlaps. It makes no continuum-limit, anomaly-free Jacobian, arbitrary off-shell Green-function, or generic physical-QFT claim.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-16.notes.md:42:The four sources and item-by-item dispositions are recorded in `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-16.source-coverage.json`. Full relevant text was inspected in Burgess, *Introduction to Effective Field Theory*, §2.2.1–2.2.5 and §2.1's redundant-interaction argument; Neubert, *Effective Field Theory and Heavy Quark Physics*, §2; Criado–Pérez-Victoria, §§2–3, §5.1 and Appendix B; and Brion, Theorems 1.23–1.24. `source-fetch-check --stamp` passed **4/4** full-text fetches with no failure or drop. Burgess/Neubert support EFT dimensions, fixed-order operators and leading-EOM conventions; Criado–Pérez-Victoria supplies the exact regulator/Jacobian/source/LSZ caveats and higher-order warning; Brion supports only the imported Reynolds/complete-reducibility input. None is substituted for the local finite-space, quotient, variational, or LSZ conditional proofs.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-16.notes.md:72:Claim and conventions: for the finite rational $G$-module $W_D$ and its $G$-stable relation span, the invariant quotient is canonically the invariant part of the raw quotient, using the exactness lemma under full AC. A specified boundary functional annihilates compactly supported total divergences. A left Euler derivative for odd fields and ordinary Euler derivative for even fields is defined by the first-variation identity. For a $G$-equivariant, parity-compatible, compact-support-preserving local variation $F$ and finite formal action $S_\epsilon=S_0+\cdots+\epsilon^NS_N$, the explicit map $\phi\mapsto\phi-\epsilon^kF$ is constructed to be invertible modulo $\epsilon^{N+1}$ and changes the action by $-\epsilon^k\mathcal I(F^a\mathcal E_a^{(0)})+O(\epsilon^{k+1})$. It removes the matching EOM term at order $k$ while retaining the higher-order terms generated by the full pullback. This proves action-level fixed-order equivalence only.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-16.notes.md:82:Claim and conventions: under full AC, a local identity-leading formal field-coordinate map, an exact regulated change-of-variables identity including its Jacobian, a source transformed by the same map, and a common limit with stable simple one-particle poles, the normalized source functionals and their normalized joint-residue amplitudes agree coefficientwise through finite order $N$. The theorem states the LSZ pole factorization and mass-shell convention $s=-\eta^{\mu\nu}p_\mu p_\nu$ with $\eta=(-,+,+,+)$; it excludes dropped Jacobians, unchanged sources, discarded higher-order terms, unstable external states, and nonexistent limits. It does not assert equality of off-shell action expressions.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-19.notes.md:61:The run-wide item dependency check examined 154 items across 110 pages and reports 60 errors outside batch 19: 58 empty scaffold inventories and two existing level mismatches. Empty pages are aqft-eft-operators, aqft-eft-operators-examples, aqft-eft-matching-running, aqft-eft-matching-running-examples, aqft-smeft-heft, aqft-smeft-heft-examples, aqft-eft-amplitudes, aqft-eft-amplitudes-examples, qftx-susy-n1-superspace-and-actions, qftx-susy-n1-superspace-and-actions-examples, qftx-susy-extended-actions, qftx-susy-extended-actions-examples, qftx-susy-ward-and-nonrenormalization, qftx-susy-ward-and-nonrenormalization-examples, qftx-susy-moduli-and-dualities, qftx-susy-moduli-and-dualities-examples, qftx-susy-breaking-and-phenomenology, qftx-susy-breaking-and-phenomenology-examples, qftx-susy-scft-and-frontier, qftx-susy-scft-and-frontier-examples, qftx-p-form-symmetries, qftx-p-form-symmetries-examples, qftx-two-group-symmetry-backgrounds, qftx-two-group-symmetry-backgrounds-examples, qftx-noninvertible-symmetries, qftx-noninvertible-symmetries-examples, qftx-finite-symmetry-gauging-physics, qftx-finite-symmetry-gauging-physics-examples, qftx-thooft-anomalies, qftx-thooft-anomalies-examples, qftx-global-anomalies-inflow, qftx-global-anomalies-inflow-examples, qftx-anomaly-matching-and-frontier, qftx-anomaly-matching-and-frontier-examples, aqft-eft-anomalies, aqft-eft-anomalies-examples, aqft-susy-effective-theories, aqft-susy-effective-theories-examples, aqft-eft-experimental-inference, aqft-eft-experimental-inference-examples, qftx-susy-backgrounds, qftx-susy-backgrounds-examples, qftx-qexact-field-theory-localization, qftx-qexact-field-theory-localization-examples, qftx-s3-partition-functions, qftx-s3-partition-functions-examples, qftx-s4-partition-functions, qftx-s4-partition-functions-examples, qftx-instanton-localization-physics, qftx-instanton-localization-physics-examples, qftx-bps-solitons-monopoles, qftx-bps-solitons-monopoles-examples, qftx-physical-hall-bps-wall-crossing, qftx-physical-hall-bps-wall-crossing-examples, qftx-spectral-networks, and qftx-spectral-networks-examples. The mismatched items are lem-qftx-compact-manifold-cohomology-positive-ideal-nilpotent (recorded level 0, computed 1) and lem-qftx-borel-base-is-paracompact-of-cw-type (recorded level 0, computed 2). These unrelated pages and items were not altered.
