research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:5:Owned pair: **qftx-finite-symmetry-gauging** and **qftx-finite-symmetry-gauging-examples**, category **quantum-field-theory-mathematics**, mathematics library. The complete design at **research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md** § “Finite Groupoid Gauging and Gluing” (lines 191–201) calls for a finite background field groupoid, cocycle-weighted gauging sum, gauge invariance, and a declared gluing law. The matching A/B rows in **research/plan-spec.json** and the batch-14 manifest agree on IDs, titles, order 970, category/library, A requiring **qftx-two-group-cochains**, and B requiring A. No design/plan conflict was found. The empty item arrays were planning placeholders. The owner direction and this dispatch control over stale scaffold-only or page-summary wording; both authored page bodies remain empty.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:7:The batch-level dependency record assigns batch 14 dependency level 1 with requires ["13"]. The authored item DAG is recorded below after all items are complete. The item plan names **def-aqft-background-gauging-data** and **thm-aqft-finite-group-gauging**; the B examples are additional assigned examples, not suppliers to another page.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:11:Before using the required page-13 input, called **loadStep1Record** and **step1Decision** for the current run. Both current records exist and return closed true: **def-aqft-two-group-background** is ready with hash a2634896ce546ad19ae337a7e2ec04413ae89c8c106f88e4efb2091382cf5acb, and **thm-aqft-two-group-background-consistency** is ready with hash 0ca4f3dc61c89dfd32c393dc2fc1e291d7c3b2d58aa0b1502d89d52ab70c7aaa. These are Step-1 authoring-readiness records, not independent proof acceptance.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:15:There is also an automorphism-interface question for the proposed use in a normalized gauging sum. If arrows are identified solely by their induced maps on cochains, then on a one-vertex complex with trivial A there is a unique background and all vertex labels g in G induce the same map; that convention gives a trivial automorphism group. The usual finite gauge groupoid over a point is BG and has automorphism group G. The current theorem does not settle whether equal induced maps retain separate gauge labels or how higher gauge-of-gauge data enter the automorphism weight. This is a material interface uncertainty for the intended two-group gauging instance.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:17:The assigned definition records the two-group specialization only conditionally and keeps the general finite-groupoid datum explicit. No current page-13 conclusion is claimed as proved. A corrected local proof of the page-13 composition/coherence result and an explicit automorphism convention are the smallest missing suppliers. They belong on the A page **qftx-two-group-cochains** or, if a full finite two-group homotopy quotient is needed, in a new mathematics A/B prerequisite pair placed before **qftx-finite-symmetry-gauging**. This batch does not edit the supplier. The affected readiness records for this batch will therefore be escalated after all available authoring and checks are complete.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:23:- **def-qftx-finite-flat-connection-groupoid** and **thm-qftx-finite-groupoid-gluing** were also inspected. They concern ordinary finite G flat connections and an untwisted finite BF theory; the gluing theorem does not cover the proposed two-group field groupoid or a cocycle action. They remain contextual and are not claimed as direct suppliers for this pair.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:25:The proposed inventory marks the finite-group-BF reuse edges as nonlogical context candidates and lists no active item supplier edges for this pair. This authoring uses only the exact generic integration and homotopy-pullback interfaces after checking their current statements and proofs; the ordinary flat-connection and untwisted gluing conclusions are not transferred to a two-group model.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:31:Read Freed–Quinn, §2, PDF pp. 8–11, including Lemma 2.4 and Theorem 2.13. The complete argument tracks boundary bundle identifications, automorphism stabilizers, the induced measure, and the cocycle-weighted gluing law. Its model is a finite ordinary group, not a proof of a two-group field-groupoid interface.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:33:Read Dijkgraaf–Witten, §§6.2 and 6.4–6.5, PDF pp. 22–30, including equations (6.8)–(6.9) and (6.24)–(6.27). It fixes the finite 3D cocycle action, ordered simplex conventions, and the closed-manifold scope of its gauge-invariance argument. Its finite 3D construction supports the bounded example only; it does not prove a general higher-group result.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:37:## Completed item: def-aqft-background-gauging-data
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:39:Defines a finite background field groupoid with its automorphism groups retained, a U(1)-valued degree-zero cocycle/action weight, and the normalized sum over isomorphism classes weighted by reciprocal automorphism order. It records the finite two-group cochain/gauge formulas as a conditional candidate instance; the existing page-13 consistency theorem and automorphism interpretation remain open as described above. Direct dependencies are **def-aqft-two-group-background**, **thm-aqft-two-group-background-consistency**, and **def-qftx-finite-groupoid-integration**; its in-run dependency level is 2. The complete generic finite-groupoid interface and exact conditional supplier excerpts are in the item and proof contract.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:43:Proves gauge invariance and the finite weighted gluing identity for finite groupoids when the restriction comparison is an equivalence to the homotopy pullback and the cocycle/action weight factors across the gluing. The proof establishes the orbit-stabilizer formula for homotopy-pullback objects, computes each boundary homotopy-fiber integral, and matches the two finite sums term by term. Direct dependencies are **def-aqft-background-gauging-data**, **def-qftx-finite-groupoid-integration**, and **def-qftx-finite-homotopy-pullback**; its in-run level is 3. The proof does not transfer ordinary finite-group flat-connection gluing to the two-group model; that instance remains subject to the conditional definition and open page-13 interface.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:57:Recomputed the assigned item closure against the current full run manifest index. No cycle or level mismatch occurs in this closure: **def-aqft-background-gauging-data** level 2; **thm-aqft-finite-group-gauging** level 3; point and C2-character examples level 3; C2 gluing example level 4. Batch 14 remains level 1 with prerequisite batch 13. A full-run item-index scan also reports 76 empty scaffold inventories in unrelated pages; none lies in this batch's dependency closure.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:61:The cross-batch dependency file is a JSON array with three rows: the required page-13 page edge is open; the inspected finite 2-group Definition item edge is verified; the consistency-theorem item edge is open. The verified row records only the scoped statement/readiness check. It does not imply independent proof approval.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-14.notes.md:73:The remaining Step-1 escalations are the exact two-group consistency proof gap and automorphism-convention ambiguity recorded above. The generic finite-groupoid theorem and its examples have complete conditional/local arguments; they do not claim the unresolved two-group specialization is proved.
