+# Batch 38 current authoring notes
+
+## Inventory and design
+
+Owned pair: `qftx-two-group-symmetry-backgrounds` / `qftx-two-group-symmetry-backgrounds-examples`, order 994, category `advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry`, physical library. The A page will contain `def-aqft-two-group-symmetry-realization` and `pthm-aqft-two-group-background-coupling`; the B page will contain finite-regulator examples. The exact scope is to consume finite mathematical background consistency, define physical coupling/observables, and keep a Postnikov background constraint distinct from an anomaly.
+
+## Plan comparison
+
+The current batch manifest and the selected `plan-spec.json` records agree on both page IDs, titles, A/B pairing, category, library and page prerequisites. The canonical plan has empty item arrays because these are authoring placeholders; the assigned future item IDs and contracts are the matching entries in `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/proposed-inventory.json`. The batch dependency-level file puts batch 38 at level 5 after batches 13 and 37, matching the cochain-mathematics and p-form page edges. Batch 37 in turn requires pages in batches 2 and 36; these are transitive page prerequisites, not extra cross-batch page-review rows. The direct use of batch 36's `def-aqft-topological-defect` in the physical realization item is recorded separately as a verified item interface edge. No design/plan conflict was found.
+
+## Exact prerequisites inspected
+
+Readiness was checked with `loadStep1Record` and `step1Decision` for the current run before recording any escalation:
+
+- `def-aqft-two-group-background` (batch 13, item level 0): actual cochain and gauge-transformation definition inspected; its existing Step 1 row says `ready`, but the current carrier hash is stale.
+- `thm-aqft-two-group-background-consistency` (batch 13, item level 1): full current conditional statement and four-cocycle proof inspected; its existing Step 1 row says `ready`, but the current carrier hash is stale.
+- `def-aqft-finite-background-two-groupoid` (batch 13, item level 2): current raw 1-arrow/2-arrow, composition, associator, units, relative boundary and stabilizer definitions inspected; no Step 1 readiness record exists.
+- `thm-aqft-finite-background-two-groupoid-coherence` (batch 13, item level 3): complete current proof inspected, including hom-category/interchange, associator naturality and pentagon, reverses, relative closure and stabilizer counts; no Step 1 readiness record exists. Its proof is conditional on the exact preceding definition and the consistency theorem.
+- `def-aqft-topological-defect` (batch 36, item level 0): the full current definition was inspected; it supplies selected-model field/configuration/correlation data and the exact smooth embedded defect/isotopy-invariance interface used by the realization definition. `step1Decision` reports a current ready record for this item. This is a scoped interface check, not independent proof approval.
+- `def-aqft-p-form-global-symmetry` (batch 37, item level 1): the carrier appeared during authoring. Its full definition and Step 1 row were inspected; `step1Decision` returns current-ready. It depends on the already current `def-aqft-topological-defect`. For p=1 it provides the exact group-like support/charge/background interface; the two-group consumer states the explicit modified cochain and gauge laws.
+
+The owner direction says the batch-13 supplier reviewer owns the higher groupoid repair and that batch 38 must inspect its actual interface or keep the unresolved prerequisite explicit. The current higher groupoid statement/proof is available and has been inspected; the remaining blockers are current readiness hashes/records, not a status label or an assumed acceptance. Root owns reconciling those records. The p-form carrier has since appeared and its current interface matches our use. Authoring continues against the exact math supplier statements, with affected items conditional and final Step 1 disposition escalated until the batch-13 records are current.
+
+## Source reading
+
+Two independent full-text treatments were inspected:
+
+- Benini, Córdova and Hsin, *On 2-Group Global Symmetries and Their Anomalies*: arXiv PDF, §2.3 “2-Group Bundles and F-Moves”, printed pp. 18–20 / PDF pp. 19–21, equations (2.14)–(2.23); the §1.2–1.3 discussion on background fields and the Postnikov/anomaly distinction; and the §3 introduction on background-gauge variation modulo local counterterms. The cochain constraint and source/target gauge rules support the finite background interface. The article's physical defect discussion is context; the finite change-of-variables result is proved locally from the stated model assumptions.
+- Schäfer-Nameki, *ICTP Lectures on (Non-)Invertible Generalized Symmetries*: arXiv v2 PDF, §§2.5 and 2.8.1–2.8.2, printed pp. 23–33, read through the background-field formulation, Postnikov constraint, selected Spin/flavor example and the stated effect of gauging on mixed anomalies. These full lecture notes independently support the p-form background and physical 2-group conventions; their gauging discussion is not generalized into a claim that the Postnikov class itself is an anomaly.
+
