## Item checkpoint: `pthm-aqft-two-group-background-coupling`

Authored a finite-regulator theorem in `items/pthm-aqft-two-group-background-coupling.md`. Its exact claim is the finite change-of-variables identity for unnormalized correlators and partition functions under a coherent gauge-arrow bijection, given a model-specified field-independent action/measure phase and covariant observable insertions. It records the counterterm change $\chi_f\mapsto e^{iL_y}\chi_fe^{-iL_x}$ and limits the conclusion to the chosen finite model. The theorem does not compute a phase for an unspecified QFT, identify $\beta$ with an anomaly, or claim a continuum limit.

Its dependencies are the physical realization definition and the four direct mathematical interfaces `def-aqft-two-group-background`, `thm-aqft-two-group-background-consistency`, `def-aqft-finite-background-two-groupoid`, and `thm-aqft-finite-background-two-groupoid-coherence`. It is item level 5, one above its highest in-run supplier `def-aqft-two-group-symmetry-realization` at level 4. The proof has steps 1.1, 2.1 and 3.1: reindex the target sum, substitute the adopted weight/observable law, and derive the counterterm phase while distinguishing beta from the model anomaly phase. All direct suppliers are current-ready and interface-matched; the finite-model law remains an explicit conditional input. The proof contract records these steps, exact supplier excerpts, boundary cases and the finite-sum rationale for omitting a separate enumeration.

The p-form page's required earlier pages are `qftx-defects-and-topological-operators` and `qftx-gauge-geometry` (batches 36 and 2). Their transitive edges are carried through batch 37; only the directly used topological-defect item is an item row in this batch's cross-batch file. The finite cochain model does not use the principal-connection interface from the gauge-geometry page, so no item-level dependency on it is asserted.

